# Development Workflow

Work on one phase at a time.

Do not jump ahead to future phases unless explicitly instructed.

Before modifying files:

1. Inspect the existing project structure.
2. Read the relevant files.
3. Understand the current implementation.
4. Identify the smallest required change.

After modifying files:

1. Run appropriate Django checks.
2. Run relevant tests when available.
3. Verify the affected functionality.
4. Report what changed.
5. Report any errors or remaining issues.

Do not claim that something works unless it has been verified.

Do not rewrite working code unnecessarily.

Do not add dependencies without a clear reason.

If an error occurs:

1. Read the complete error.
2. Identify the root cause.
3. Fix the underlying problem.
4. Re-run the relevant check.

Do not randomly modify unrelated files.

Do not implement features that were not requested.